# Part III — Separate Geometry from Timing

This is particularly important.

Burning is not merely a static ball-covering problem.

The radii are ordered:

$$
q-1,q-2,\ldots,1,0.
$$

Therefore a source placed early has a larger future radius than a source placed late.

Determine whether the obstruction can arise from:

$$
\text{pure geometric covering difficulty}
$$

or from

$$
\text{temporal incompatibility of the balls}.
$$

Try to construct examples where:

* a static collection of balls of the correct radii can cover T;
* but their temporal ordering prevents the corresponding burning sequence;

or determine whether such a distinction disappears for trees.

This may reveal the actual invariant needed for the proof.

